        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A regular dodecagon inscribed in a circle of radius 5 cm.",
          "worked": "Draw a circle of radius 5 cm. With compasses set to 5 cm, step around the circumference six times and join consecutive points to construct the regular hexagon, as in question 4. Mark each side's midpoint. Join opposite midpoints and extend each line to the circle. Join the twelve circumference points in the stated order. Each original $60^\\circ$ central sector is bisected, giving twelve equal $30^\\circ$ sectors and hence twelve equal sides.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p27-q5-a-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"page 27 question 5a constructed answer\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont},line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0) circle (2);\n\\foreach \\n/\\a in {A/120,G/90,B/60,H/30,C/0,I/-30,D/-60,J/-90,E/-120,K/-150,F/180,L/150}{\\coordinate (\\n) at (\\a:2);\\node at (\\a:2.35) {$\\n$};}\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (G)--(J) (H)--(K) (I)--(L);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (A)--(G)--(B)--(H)--(C)--(I)--(D)--(J)--(E)--(K)--(F)--(L)--cycle;\n\\fill (0,0) circle (1pt);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0)--(C) node[midway,below] {$5\\text{ cm}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
