        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Label the vertices $1,2,3,\\ldots,12$ clockwise (with 12 as the topmost vertex). What have you constructed?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A clock face.",
          "worked": "Put 12 at the top, then 1 to 11 clockwise at successive vertices. The twelve equally spaced positions form a clock face.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p27-q5-b-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"page 27 question 5b clock-face answer\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont},line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\foreach \\n in {1,...,12}{\\coordinate (V\\n) at ({90-30*\\n}:2);\\node at ({90-30*\\n}:2.35) {$\\n$};}\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (V1)--(V2)--(V3)--(V4)--(V5)--(V6)--(V7)--(V8)--(V9)--(V10)--(V11)--(V12)--cycle;\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
